(ned TCP CAL -- ONE TOUCH of the two-touch pivot-length measurement)
(Operator 2026-08-05, one button: touch 1 probes wherever the operator has)
(parked the needle over the puck. The operator then tilts A on the MPG so)
(the needle still lands on the puck -- that hand step is the whole point,)
(it is what guarantees the touch -- and touch 2 probes again.)
(The rod carries a NEEDLE POINT on the spindle axis, so the contact IS the)
(tool tip at any tilt and no rod-radius term enters the math.)
(THE PUCK STAYS UP BETWEEN THE TWO TOUCHES. Its pop-up repeatability would)
(otherwise land straight in dZ, which IS the measurement.)
(INCREMENTAL BY DESIGN. This took an absolute Z floor computed in the GUI)
(from stat.actual_position minus stat.g5x_offset. stat reported zero)
(offsets while the interpreter had G54 live at Z -512.205, so a "work")
(target of -447 became machine -959 and motion refused it: "Probe move on)
(line 44 would exceed Z negative limit", instantly, without moving.)
(G91 has no frame to get wrong -- "30 mm down from here" is the same)
(instruction in every coordinate system, and it is what the operator)
(actually asked for. Every absolute Z below is derived from #5063, which)
(is reported in whatever frame the interpreter is really in, so it agrees)
(with itself by construction.)
(Args: #1 = plunge depth in mm, positive, measured from where we sit)
(      #2 = 1 to deploy the puck first, 0 when it is already up)
(      #3 = hover height above the contact to retract to)
o<tcp_touch> sub
  #<plunge> = #1
  #<deploy> = #2
  #<hover>  = #3
  #<fast>   = 200.0
  #<latch>  = 10.0
  #<back>   = 1.0
  #<trav>   = 1000.0

  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, TCP CAL: switch to MM first - this routine is metric)
  o10 endif

  o15 if [#<plunge> LE 0]
    (abort, TCP CAL: plunge depth must be positive)
  o15 endif

  ; the F slider must not scale a probe: cal_probe_center learned this when
  ; 150% turned programmed 200 into 300 (2026-08-03)
  M50 P0

  o20 if [#<deploy> GT 0]
    M64 P3
    G4 P1.5
  o20 endif

  ; FIXED PLUNGE, straight down from wherever the operator parked. Nothing
  ; here predicts where contact should be: the deviation from expectation
  ; IS the measurement. A needle not over the puck simply runs out of
  ; plunge and reports no contact.
  G91
  G38.2 Z-#<plunge> F[#<fast>]
  G1 Z[#<back>] F[#<trav>]
  G38.2 Z-[#<back> + 1.0] F[#<latch>]
  #<zt> = #5063
  #<at> = #5064
  ; release PROVEN before any ordinary move -- see ca_touch.ngc
  G38.5 Z[#<back> + 1.0] F[#<latch>]
  ; back to absolute ONLY against #5063, the interpreter own reading, so
  ; the frame cancels
  G90
  G1 Z[#<zt> + #<hover>] F[#<trav>]
  M50 P1
  (DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"ned_controls"}.tcp_cal_point{#<zt>, #<at>}])
o<tcp_touch> endsub
M2
